ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":114,"prev":116,"next":119,"titles":121,"firmware":290},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":9,"order":10,"path":11,"context":12,"summary":17,"status":18,"firmware":19,"facts":27,"procedures":71,"parameters":87,"related":94,"body":97,"sources":98,"official_url":31,"controls":109},"sampler.sample-library","Sample library",[5,6,7,8],"sample browser","browse samples","load a sample","sample preview","sampler",60,"knowledge/manual/units/sampler/sample-library.md",{"modes":13,"screens":15},[14],"instrument",[16],"sample library","`shift + sample` opens the library of every sample on the unit: pick a folder, hear each sample as you land on it, and click an encoder to load it into the sampler.","outdated-in-guide",{"min":20,"changed_in":21,"guide_version":23,"verified_on":26},"1.0.9",[22,23,24,25],"1.1.0","1.1.15","1.1.17","1.2.0",null,[28,33,36,39,42,46,49,54,58,62,66],{"id":29,"text":30,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"what","The library holds every sample on the unit and loads any of them into any of the three samplers.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sample#sample-folder","official",{"id":34,"text":35,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"preview","In the library a sample plays as soon as it is selected; `stop` ends the preview.",{"id":37,"text":38,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"enter","Clicking any encoder opens a subfolder or loads the selected sample; subfolder names are in square brackets.",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"new-folders","New folders are made on a computer, inside the samples folder, in MTP mode.",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":45,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"user-folder","Samples you record on the unit are kept in the library's user folder, which a computer sees as samples → user in MTP mode.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/how-to#how-to-load-samples",{"id":47,"text":48,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"key-controls","Up to OS 1.1.33, for the drum sampler and multisampler, `M2` and `M3` step through filled keys and `M4` clears a key without deleting its file.",{"id":50,"text":51,"source":52,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":26,"confidence":53},"key-controls-os12","On OS 1.2 the guide gives the library browser these module keys: `M1` and `M2` step through the filled keys (drum sampler and multisampler), `M3` renames a sample of your own (never a factory one), `M4` deletes it from the library once you confirm (`M4` confirms, `M3` cancels) and `shift + M4` clears the key. Renaming itself is older (a July 2026 changelog entry); the earlier guide just names no key for it.","docs/research/79b-os12-small-features.md#4-sample-library-keys-guide-v120","community-verified",{"id":55,"text":56,"source":57,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"from-key","Holding a keyboard key and pressing `sample` browses samples for that key.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.0",{"id":59,"text":60,"source":61,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"preset-samples","Samples used by your own presets are gathered in one group.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.15",{"id":63,"text":64,"source":65,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"preview-setting","A system setting controls the sample preview; the changelog does not say where it is.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.17",{"id":67,"text":68,"source":69,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":70},"take-names","Takes in the user folder are named project-note-track.wav, such as unnamed-f2-5.wav, and a library take uses F2 and the current track number (community, OS 1.x).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",[72],{"id":73,"goal":74,"preconditions":75,"steps":76,"result":26,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confiden